event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"item_id":"rs_986140","output_index":0,"sequence_number":614,"summary_index":0,"text":"We need to implement the application meeting requirements. The previous submission failed to show alert with role 'alert' containing the required text when blank/whitespace project name submitted.\n\nWe must create a simple Node.js server using built-in http and sqlite, no external deps. Serve static HTML/JS for front-end. Use SQLite to store projects with id (INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT) and name.\n\nWe need route GET / health, GET / returns index.html, also GET /projects/:id returns project page.\n\nAlso need POST endpoint to create project: probably POST /projects with JSON body {name}. But the front-end can use form submission with fetch.\n\nNeed to ensure blank or whitespace-only name triggers alert visible with role=\"alert\" and text \"Project name is required\". Also need to not add row.\n\nProject rows should have data-testid=\"project-row\". Each row includes name and button \"Open project\". The button links to /projects/\u003cid\u003e.\n\nAlso need Projects button on project page linking back to \"/\".\n\nPersist data across restarts: Use DB_PATH env var.\n\nWe must implement using only node built-in modules, no express, no external. We'll use node:http, node:url, node:fs, node:path, node:sqlite (requires node:sqlite? Actually Node.js 22 includes experimental sqlite module? Let's assume node:sqlite is available. We'll use require('sqlite3')? But external not allowed. Node built-in sqlite is \"node:sqlite\" (experimental). Use async API.\n\nWe'll create server.js that:\n\n- reads env PORT default 8080, DB_PATH default './workboard.db' maybe.\n\n- opens sqlite db with open method.\n\n- ensure table projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL).\n\n- handle requests:\n\nif GET /health =\u003e respond JSON.\n\nif GET / =\u003e serve index.html.\n\nif GET /projects/:id =\u003e serve project.html with dynamic content? Could embed project id and name via server rendering or let front-end fetch via API.\n\nSimpler: Serve a generic project page that fetches project data via GET /api/projects/:id.\n\nThus need API routes: GET /api/projects returns list, POST /api/projects create, GET /api/projects/:id get single.\n\nRoutes: if path starts with /api/..., handle JSON.\n\nOtherwise serve static files from public directory.\n\nWe'll create public/index.html with script that fetches list, renders rows.\n\nImplement alert: we can create \u003cdiv role=\"alert\" style=\"color:red; display:none;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e and show when needed.\n\nImplement trimming: client-side will trim; if after trim empty, show alert.\n\nAlso server side should validate and not insert empty names.\n\nImplement create project via POST /api/projects with JSON body.\n\nNeed to parse request body: collect chunks, parse JSON.\n\nAll within built-in.\n\nNow need to commit and run npm start. Need package.json with start script: \"node server.js\". No dependencies.\n\nMake sure server serves static files from public directory.\n\nNow implement.\n\n","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

